WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.300
Zero dimensions: a single point. All ten strokes fall from it.

2
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.200
One dimension: write the character in front of you, stroke by stroke, and set it right.

3
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.100
The line meets itself and encloses a page.

4
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.800
Two dimensions: paper is the battlefield, the brush the soldier, ink the armor.

5
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.500
Through the page: on the back, every character is mirrored.

6
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:32.400
A Möbius strip: no left or right edge, and only one side.

7
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:37.300
The page folds along its creases into a cube.

8
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.000
Three dimensions: write a distant enemy’s character, and it flies to them.

9
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:45.500
The cube is only one cell of a tesseract.

10
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.600
By the Early Heaven trigrams: thunder, water, mountain, wind, fire, lake.

11
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.700
The eight cells become one, and you step inside.

12
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.400
Four dimensions: one more direction you cannot see.

13
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.200
Coming soon
